## File-by-File Reference

### Core Files

#### [app.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/app.py)
FastAPI server with production hardening.

| Feature | Detail |
|---|---|
| `GET /health` | Returns `{"status": "ok"}` |
| `POST /chat` | Main chat endpoint |
| Rate limiting | 20 requests/min per session_id (in-memory) |
| Env validation | Checks `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `DATABASE_URL`, `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS` on startup |
| Error handling | Global exception handler + endpoint-level try/except |

#### [main.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/main.py)
LangGraph definition and routing.

- **[chat_router(session_id, state, user_message)](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/main.py#63-92)** — main entry point
  - Loads persisted session state from DB
  - **Confirmation guard**: if `awaiting_confirmation == True`, routes directly to [handle_confirmation()](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#70-134) (bypasses graph)
  - Otherwise invokes the LangGraph
- **Graph structure**: [classify_intent](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#140-253) → conditional edges → [schedule_meeting](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#255-342) / [email_flow](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#344-406) / [normal_chat](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#448-592)

#### [nodes.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py)
All LangGraph node functions (~550 lines).

| Node | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [extract_email_node](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#32-70) | Regex-extracts email addresses from messages |
| [handle_confirmation](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#70-134) | Handles yes/no responses for email confirmation flow |
| [classify_intent_node](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#140-253) | LLM-based intent classification with sliding window memory (last 10 messages), profile injection, conversation summary, response time logging |
| [schedule_meeting_node](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#255-342) | Validates meeting fields → parses date/time to ISO → calls [create_calendar_event()](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/tools/calendar_tool.py#8-33) → returns Google Calendar link |
| [email_flow_node](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#344-406) | Extracts recipient/subject/body → sets `awaiting_confirmation=True` → asks user to confirm |
| [normal_chat_node](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/nodes.py#448-592) | Full conversational AI with Frosty persona, sliding window memory, profile injection, summary generation (every 10 messages), profile extraction via `memory.user_profile` |

#### [state.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/state.py)
TypedDict definitions for the entire state tree.

```
State
├── session: SessionInfo (session_id, user_id, etc.)
├── input: InputMessage (raw_message, audio_url, etc.)
├── intent: IntentPayload (intent, reply, meeting data, email data)
├── email_flow: EmailFlowState (draft, pending_confirmation, sent)
├── meeting_flow: MeetingFlowState (validated, availability, events)
├── voice: VoiceState
├── knowledge_base: KnowledgeBaseContext
├── model_io: ModelIOState (api_response, debug)
├── memory_keys, scratch: Dict
├── awaiting_confirmation: bool
├── recipient, subject, body: str (for email confirmation)
```

---

### Tools

#### [tools/llm_tool.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/tools/llm_tool.py)
LLM-based intent + data extraction.

- **Sliding window**: loads last 10 messages from DB as role-based context
- **Profile injection**: loads user profile after system prompt
- **Conversation summary**: injected when available
- **Company knowledge**: ground truth context
- **Response time logging**: logs elapsed seconds for every LLM call
- Returns structured JSON with [intent](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/main.py#24-27), `reply`, and extracted fields

#### [tools/calendar_tool.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/tools/calendar_tool.py)
Google Calendar integration using service account.

```python
create_calendar_event(summary, description, start_time, end_time) → str (htmlLink)
```

- Uses `google.oauth2.service_account` credentials
- Creates events on `primary` calendar
- Timezone: `Asia/Kolkata`
- Requires `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` env var pointing to service account JSON

#### [tools/email_tool.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/tools/email_tool.py)
SMTP email sender.

```python
send_email(to_email, subject, body) → bool
```

- Uses `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`, `SMTP_FROM` env vars
- TLS connection on port 587
- Returns `True`/`False` for success/failure

#### [tools/voice_tool.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/tools/voice_tool.py)
Speech-to-Text via OpenAI Whisper.

```python
transcribe_audio(base64_audio: str) → str
```

- Decodes base64 → writes temp `.wav` file → sends to `whisper-1`
- Returns transcribed text
- Raises `ValueError` on bad base64, `RuntimeError` on Whisper failure

#### [tools/tts_tool.py](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/tools/tts_tool.py)
Text-to-Speech via OpenAI TTS.

```python
generate_speech(text: str) → str (base64)
```

- Model: `gpt-4o-mini-tts`, Voice: `alloy`
- Returns base64-encoded audio (utf-8)
- Returns empty string on failure

